From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: discard cached frame when replacing video

DigitalVideoCastMember::loadVideo() replaces the decoder when its source path
changes, but previously retained the converted frame cached from the outgoing
movie.  Trek Tech reuses one cast member for detail and transit movies.  If the
new decoder has not produced its first frame before the next render, that stale
surface can be copied using the replacement movie's dimensions, yielding
stretched scanlines or a frozen first frame depending on timing.

Discard the cached frame and force one redraw whenever the source changes.
This does not alter playback timing, decoding, palettes, or normal rendering.
---
 engines/director/castmember/digitalvideo.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/director/castmember/digitalvideo.cpp b/engines/director/castmember/digitalvideo.cpp
--- a/engines/director/castmember/digitalvideo.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/castmember/digitalvideo.cpp
@@ -264,6 +264,16 @@ bool DigitalVideoCastMember::loadVideo(Common::String path) {
 		return _video ? true : false;
 	}
 
+	// A converted frame belongs to the decoder that produced it. Keeping it
+	// across a source change can make createWidget() read the old surface using
+	// the new movie's dimensions before the replacement's first frame arrives.
+	if (_lastFrame) {
+		_lastFrame->free();
+		delete _lastFrame;
+		_lastFrame = nullptr;
+	}
+	_dirty = true;
+
 	if (_video) {
 		delete _video;
 		_video = nullptr;
-- 
2.51.0
